0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#what-forge-is","title":"What Forge is"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-problem-it-exists-to-solve","title":"The problem it exists to solve"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-a-remote-cache-is","title":"What a remote cache is"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-remote-execution-is","title":"What remote execution is"},{"depth":2,"url":"#why-forge-specifically","title":"Why Forge specifically"},{"depth":2,"url":"#is-this-for-you","title":"Is this for you?"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-three-cases-worth-their-own-page","title":"The three cases worth their own page"},{"depth":2,"url":"#common-questions","title":"Common questions"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Why Forge"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"What Forge is, what a remote cache and remote execution actually do, and a 30-second check for whether your build is one that benefits."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone deciding whether to put a remote cache and\nexecution layer in front of their build, including people meeting the idea for\nthe first time. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," a working mental model of what\nForge does, and a clear yes or no for your own situation. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," about\nten minutes."]}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-forge-is","children":"What Forge is"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Forge is a ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"remote build cache"}]," and a ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"remote execution"}]," service in one\nprogram. Your build tool asks it \"have you already built this?\" and, when the\nanswer is no, \"can you build it for me over there?\" Nothing about your source\ncode changes. You point your build tool at a URL, and work that used to happen\non your machine stops happening on your machine."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["It's written in Rust, ships as a single binary that plays every role, and\nspeaks the ",["$","$L7",null,{"href":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/remote-apis","children":"Remote Execution API"}],",\nan open protocol, not a Forge invention, which is why the build tool you\nalready use can talk to it without a plugin."]}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-problem-it-exists-to-solve","children":"The problem it exists to solve"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Every build system computes the same thing twice. Once on your laptop, once in\nCI. Once for you, once for the colleague who pulled the same commit. Once\nbefore lunch, once after you reverted the change that broke it. The work is\ndeterministic, the inputs are identical, and the machine does it again anyway."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"That waste has two different shapes, and they need two different fixes."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Some work is ",["$","em",null,{"children":"redundant"}],": somebody, somewhere, already produced exactly this\noutput from exactly these inputs. The fix is a cache."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Some work is ",["$","em",null,{"children":"genuinely new"}]," but badly placed: it has to run, but it doesn't\nhave to run on the laptop you're typing on, one action at a time. The fix is to\nrun it somewhere else, in parallel, on hardware that suits it."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Forge is both fixes."}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-a-remote-cache-is","children":"What a remote cache is"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["A build is a graph of actions. Each action has inputs (source files, compiler\nflags, the compiler itself) and produces outputs. A ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"remote cache"}]," stores\nthose outputs on a server keyed by a hash of all of the inputs."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Before running an action, your build tool hashes the inputs and asks the server\nwhether it has a result for that hash. A hit means the output is downloaded\ninstead of computed. A miss means the action runs and the result is uploaded so\nthat nobody else has to run it."}],"\n","$L8","\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24"]}],"$L25"]}],["$L26","$L27"],"$L28"]}],"isPartial":"$@29","staleTime":"$2a","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L2b","isPartial":"$@2c","staleTime":"$2a","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L2d","isPartial":"$@2e","staleTime":"$2a","varyParams":"$2f"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@30","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@31"}
